# Cross-platform fixture packaging for the Event Dossier Protocol.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
#
# The freeze_manifest gate hashes artifact bytes and compares the result to the
# sha256 recorded in freeze_manifest*.json. Git stores every textual artifact in
# this directory as LF (all 454 tracked blobs were verified pure LF), but Git for
# Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its system config, so a Windows checkout
# materialises those same blobs as CRLF. A manifest whose hashes were computed
# from the Windows *working tree* therefore records CRLF-derived digests that no
# LF checkout -- Linux CI, macOS, or any clone with core.autocrlf=false -- can
# reproduce. That is exactly what happened: the manifests committed before
# 2026-08-06 were accidentally calculated from Windows CRLF working-tree bytes,
# which is why the validator suite passed locally on Windows and failed on every
# GitHub Actions run.
#
# Pinning eol=lf makes the working-tree bytes byte-identical to the committed
# blob bytes on every platform, so a hash computed anywhere is the hash CI
# verifies. Git's committed blob bytes are the canonical form.
#
# SCOPE
#
# Deliberately narrow: this file applies only to Event_Dossier_Protocol/ and
# leaves the rest of the repository's line-ending behaviour untouched. It
# changes no global or system Git configuration.

*.csv  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf

# Extensionless textual files under this directory, so nothing here is left to
# the system-wide core.autocrlf=true default.
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.gitkeep       text eol=lf
